  annotation = {中文辅助译名：基于等离子体相变材料In 3 SbTe 2 的宽带双曲热超表面},
  abstract = {(IST) that undergoes a non-volatile dielectric-to-metal phase transition during crystallization offers a fitting solution. Here, we have prepared IST-based hyperbolic thermal metasurfaces and demonstrated their capabilities to modulate thermal radiation. By laser-printing crystalline IST gratings with different fill factors on amorphous IST films, we have achieved multilevel, large-range, and polarization-dependent control of the emissivity modulation (0.07 for the crystalline phase and 0.73 for the amorphous phase) over a broad bandwidth (8-14 μm). With the convenient direct laser writing technique that supports large-scale surface patterning, we have also demonstrated promising applications of thermal anti-counterfeiting with hyperbolic thermal metasurfaces.},
}

